Data comes from OpenDART (Financial Supervisory Service), KIND (Korea Exchange), the US SEC, KIPRIS,
the National Law Information Center, KOSIS and Building HUB. Their terms apply to that data.

The scoring models follow their published formulas:
- Beneish, M. D. (1999). The Detection of Earnings Manipulation. Financial Analysts Journal.
- Altman, E. I., Hartzell, J., Peck, M. (1995). Emerging Markets Corporate Bonds: A Scoring System.
- Piotroski, J. D. (2000). Value Investing. Journal of Accounting Research.
- Sloan, R. G. (1996). Do Stock Prices Fully Reflect Information in Accruals and Cash Flows. The Accounting Review.
